[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Objective
[stderr] 
[stderr] Document and test the P0 negative boundary: local campaign start, save, and
[stderr] resume require no account identifier, token, remote profile, authorization
[stderr] role, entitlement, multiplayer, moderation, safety, or connected service.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Dependencies
[stderr] 
[stderr] R0002 supplies the core/adapter dependency seam and R0004 supplies the local
[stderr] campaign state envelope. They are implementation dependencies. Retain
[stderr] GATE-0006 / DEC-0006: no connected feature may be implemented until its scope,
[stderr] privacy, security, operational, cost, and failure-mode decisions are approved.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Ownership
[stderr] 
[stderr] - `docs/security-boundary.md`.
[stderr] - `tests/core/connected-scope-exclusion.*`.
[stderr] - The future connected-service approval checklist and local-slot identity
[stderr]   contract.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Required behaviour
[stderr] 
[stderr] State that the local browser profile is the P0 player boundary, not an account
[stderr] or authorization guarantee. The local campaign is the source of truth and has
[stderr] no remote profile, analytics stream, purchase ledger, match state, cloud
[stderr] backup, role, privilege, or entitlement. Local slot selection is an opaque
[stderr] local reference only and must not contain identity, token, privilege, or remote
[stderr] profile fields.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Add negative contract tests and a static boundary scan for P0 foundation
[stderr] modules. They must fail on identity/token/role/entitlement fields, network or
[stderr] server clients, sign-in/OAuth/sync paths, multiplayer/safety/moderation APIs,
[stderr] purchase flows, or remote campaign authority. Treat future replication, if
[stderr] ever approved, as a separate optional mirror rather than campaign truth.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] 
[stderr] Responsive web and installed PWA use the same local-slot contract and same
[stderr] connected-scope exclusion. PWA installation, cache, and browser-origin storage
[stderr] do not imply identity, authorization, sync, or a remote service. No target
[stderr] obtains a distinct connected implementation path.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Non-goals
[stderr] 
[stderr] Do not implement sign-in, OAuth, accounts, profiles, tokens, roles,
[stderr] authorization, synchronization, server APIs, analytics transport, multiplayer,
[stderr] moderation, reporting, purchases, entitlements, cloud saves, remote
[stderr] diagnostics, or security claims about a device owner. Do not create product
[stderr] assets, audio, or connected-service configuration.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Asset assessment
[stderr] 
[stderr] `asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this is documentation and negative test
[stderr] coverage for an architectural exclusion. Do not create or reserve incidental
[stderr] visual, source, audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or
[stderr] other product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Verification
[stderr] 
[stderr] - Run a static scan across P0 foundation modules for prohibited identity,
[stderr]   token, privilege, entitlement, and network/server-client fields or imports.
[stderr] - Run negative fixtures that attempt prohibited connected-scope configuration
[stderr]   and prove the contract rejects or does not expose it.
[stderr] - Verify start, local save, and local resume fixtures require only a local slot
[stderr]   reference and no remote request or account data.
[stderr] - Review `docs/security-boundary.md` against the exclusion list and record
[stderr]   GATE-0006 / DEC-0006 as retained for any future connected proposal.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Evidence
[stderr] 
[stderr] Retain static-scan and negative-fixture results, local start/save/resume test
[stderr] output showing no remote request, the security-boundary review, and the future
[stderr] connected-service approval checklist with its retained gate.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] 
[stderr] - P0 start, save, and resume expose no identity, token, role, entitlement,
[stderr]   remote-profile, or network-client field or dependency.
[stderr] - Negative tests prevent connected-service scope from entering P0 foundation
[stderr]   modules for both web and PWA delivery paths.
[stderr] - Any future connected work remains outside campaign truth and blocked by
[stderr]   GATE-0006 / DEC-0006 rather than implicitly approved.
