th\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0010.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0010\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0002\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No final artwork, fonts, or icons; semantic tokens only and prohibit incidental assets.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"non-colour cues\",\"reduced motion values\",\"GATE-0002,GATE-0004 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and await numeric design decisions\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json:42:    {\"id\":\"R0011\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0011\",\"title\":\"Create original-content provenance control\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0005\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0011.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0011\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets are created; this contract defines provenance controls for later asset-required work.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"missing provenance rejected\",\"human creative review recorded\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json:43:    {\"id\":\"R0012\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0012\",\"title\":\"Document foundation architecture and recovery boundaries\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0004\",\"R0006\",\"R0008\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0012\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0006\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; developer-documentation closure only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"all foundation ownership/dependencies/gates cross-checked\",\"does not claim release readiness\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this documentation contract\"}\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json-44-  ]\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json-45-}\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"git status --short projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4 && sed -n '1,260p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0004.md && sed -n '1,260p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0008.md && sed -n '1,260p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/TEMPLATE.md && rg -n -C 3 'IMP-0004|IMP-0008' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue*.json && rg -n -C 2 'F014|runbook|manifest' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning -g '*.md'\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n exited 1 in 0ms:\n?? projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/\n---\ntask_id: R0004\nsequence: 4\ntitle: Define deterministic campaign state and command contract\ndependencies: R0002,R0003\nrequirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0003,REQ-0004,REQ-0006,NFR-0002,NFR-0010\nsource_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract,specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-0004\nauthoring_batch: B0003\nfactory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nasset_impact: not_applicable\nasset_ids:\nasset_brief: No assets; state envelopes deliberately exclude authored content.\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids:\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nDefine the immutable, versioned shared campaign-state, command, result, event,\nrevision, interaction-ID, and deterministic-RNG contracts needed to validate\nlegal transitions. This foundation defines envelopes and invariants only; it\ndoes not introduce a feature state machine or authored campaign values.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nR0002 provides the shared-core/adapter seam and R0003 provides deterministic\nfixtures. They are implementation dependencies, not authoring blockers.\nRetain GATE-0004: concrete party and content shapes remain unapproved.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- `src/core/{state,commands,events,invariants,rng}/`.\n- The versioned campaign-snapshot envelope and deterministic RNG state.\n- The public core command, state, event, result, revision, and interaction-ID\n  interfaces, plus `tests/core/contract.*`.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\nMake state transitions pure and explicit: a command carries an expected\ncampaign revision and stable interaction/action ID; processing returns either\na typed rejection with no mutation or ordered state/events with a new revision.\nValidate command shape, session state, identifiers, availability, eligibility,\npredicates, and expected revision before any transition. Invariant helpers\nmust reject invalid state and preserve the prior immutable state.\n\nRecord deterministic RNG seed/state at safe boundaries. Require idempotency for\nretries: a duplicate interaction ID or acknowledged durable transition returns\nits prior result without a second reward, checkpoint, or revision-changing\ntransition. Process one command at a time per active campaign and reject stale\nwriters so visibility changes, repeated input, and concurrent tabs cannot\ninterleave a transition.\n\n## Web and PWA differences\n\nWeb and PWA adapters submit the same shared command envelopes and consume the\nsame state/event results. Platform adapters may debounce controls and manage a\nlocal slot lease/read-only warning, but neither gains authority to mutate state\ndirectly. Installation, cache lifecycle, and storage-driver work are outside\nthis contract.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nDo not author content values; implement combat, inventory, quest, exploration,\nor UI state machines; select party shapes; implement a save driver or cache;\nadd account, identity, token, role, network, or remote state; or create assets,\naudio, maps, dialogue, or reference-derived content.\n\n## Asset assessment\n\n`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: these serializable state and interface\ncontracts deliberately exclude authored content. Do not create or reserve\nincidental visual, source, audio, font, icon, illustration, texture, sprite,\nmap, or other product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Use R0003 deterministic fixtures to prove invalid commands leave the exact\n  prior state unchanged and stale revisions reject without mutation.\n- Prove a duplicate interaction ID returns the recorded prior outcome and\n  produces no additional durable transition.\n- Exercise controlled RNG state twice and compare state/event results.\n- Exercise sequential command handling and a stale-writer fixture without\n  selecting a browser-storage implementation.\n- Record GATE-0004 as retained before adding concrete party/content shapes.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRetain contract-test output for invalid, stale, duplicate, deterministic-RNG,\nand serialized transition cases, plus the public envelope/invariant inventory\nand the retained GATE-0004 record.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Invalid or stale commands cannot mutate campaign state.\n- Duplicate interaction IDs are idempotent and cause no extra durable\n  transition.\n- State, command, result, event, revision, and RNG contracts are shared-core\n  only, versioned where serialized, and independent of concrete content,\n  persistence drivers, or connected scope.\n---\ntask_id: R0008\nsequence: 8\ntitle: Bound P0 identity, authorization, and connected-service exclusions\ndependencies: R0002,R0004\nrequirement_ids: REQ-0013,REQ-0014,REQ-0015,NFR-0012\nsource_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-0008\nauthoring_batch: B0003\nfactory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nasset_impact: not_applicable\nasset_ids:\nasset_brief: No assets; a negative scope boundary.\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids:\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nDocument and test the P0 negative boundary: local campaign start, save, and\nresume require no account identifier, token, remote profile, authorization\nrole, entitlement, multiplayer, moderation, safety, or connected service.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nR0002 supplies the core/adapter dependency seam and R0004 supplies the local\ncampaign state envelope. They are implementation dependencies. Retain\nGATE-0006 / DEC-0006: no connected feature may be implemented until its scope,\nprivacy, security, operational, cost, and failure-mode decisions are approved.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- `docs/security-boundary.md`.\n- `tests/core/connected-scope-exclusion.*`.\n- The future connected-service approval checklist and local-slot identity\n  contract.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\nState that the local browser profile is the P0 player boundary, not an account\nor authorization guarantee. The local campaign is the source of truth and has\nno remote profile, analytics stream, purchase ledger, match state, cloud\nbackup, role, privilege, or entitlement. Local slot selection is an opaque\nlocal reference only and must not contain identity, token, privilege, or remote\nprofile fields.\n\nAdd negative contract tests and a static boundary scan for P0 foundation\nmodules. They must fail on identity/token/role/entitlement fields, network or\nserver clients, sign-in/OAuth/sync paths, multiplayer/safety/moderation APIs,\npurchase flows, or remote campaign authority. Treat future replication, if\never approved, as a separate optional mirror rather than campaign truth.\n\n## Web and PWA differences\n\nResponsive web and installed PWA use the same local-slot contract and same\nconnected-scope exclusion. PWA installation, cache, and browser-origin storage\ndo not imply identity, authorization, sync, or a remote service. No target\nobtains a distinct connected implementation path.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nDo not implement sign-in, OAuth, accounts, profiles, tokens, roles,\nauthorization, synchronization, server APIs, analytics transport, multiplayer,\nmoderation, reporting, purchases, entitlements, cloud saves, remote\ndiagnostics, or security claims about a device owner. Do not create product\nassets, audio, or connected-service configuration.\n\n## Asset assessment\n\n`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this is documentation and negative test\ncoverage for an architectural exclusion. Do not create or reserve incidental\nvisual, source, audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or\nother product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Run a static scan across P0 foundation modules for prohibited identity,\n  token, privilege, entitlement, and network/server-client fields or imports.\n- Run negative fixtures that attempt prohibited connected-scope configuration\n  and prove the contract rejects or does not expose it.\n- Verify start, local save, and local resume fixtures require only a local slot\n  reference and no remote request or account data.\n- Review `docs/security-boundary.md` against the exclusion list and record\n  GATE-0006 / DEC-0006 as retained for any future connected proposal.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRetain static-scan and negative-fixture results, local start/save/resume test\noutput showing no remote request, the security-boundary review, and the future\nconnected-service approval checklist with its retained gate.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- P0 start, save, and resume expose no identity, token, role, entitlement,\n  remote-profile, or network-client field or dependency.\n- Negative tests prevent connected-service scope from entering P0 foundation\n  modules for both web and PWA delivery paths.\n- Any future connected work remains outside campaign truth and blocked by\n  GATE-0006 / DEC-0006 rather than implicitly approved.\nsed: projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/TEMPLATE.md: No such file or directory\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4 | rg '(\"'^|/)(R000[1-9]|R0010)'\"\\\\.md\"'$|TEMPLATE'\"\\\\.md\"'$|F014'\"\\\\.md\"'$|runbook.*(valid|check)|implementation-catalogue'\"' && rg -n -C 6 '\\\"id\\\": \\\"IMP-0004\\\"|\\\"id\\\": \\\"IMP-0008\\\"|IMP-0004|IMP-0008' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json && find projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks -maxdepth 1 -type f -print | sort\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0008.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0002.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0003.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0004.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0010.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\n5-  \"scope\": \"P0 is an original, offline-capable 2D single-player fantasy RPG delivered through a shared web core and a PWA delivery adapt